Show snouty's settings, and trust or deny a project settings file

`settings show` prints the settings that snouty resolved, and the settings files
it read. `settings trust` and `settings deny` decide whether snouty uses a
project settings file (./.snouty.toml).

A project settings file can set any setting, including base_url, https_proxy and
repository. snouty sends your API key to base_url, sends its requests through
https_proxy, and pushes your images to repository, so a settings file from a
cloned repository could send your credentials or images to another server. Read
the file, or run `snouty --settings ./.snouty.toml settings show` to see the
settings that snouty would resolve with it, before you trust it. If you do not
want snouty to use the file, run `snouty settings deny`.

Examples:
  snouty --settings ./.snouty.toml settings show
  snouty settings trust
  snouty settings deny

Usage: snouty settings [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  show   Print the settings that snouty resolved
  trust  Use a project settings file while its content stays the same
  deny   Ignore a project settings file
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
